<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="What is retopology?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Building a clean, lower-polygon mesh over a detailed sculpt" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Adding subdivision levels to a sculpt">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Painting textures onto a model">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Rigging a character for animation">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="It's good practice to establish large forms at low subdivision levels before adding fine detail.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">Why might you bake the details of a high-resolution sculpt into a normal map?</p>
  <p>So a lower-polygon mesh that can be animated or used in real time keeps the look of the fine detail, without the cost of the sculpt's millions of polygons.</p>
</self-check>
